---
import "../../styles/global.css";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />

    <link
      rel="icon"
      type="image/png"
      href="/images/kasodi-favicon.png"
    />

    <title>Small Details That Change a Room | KASODI</title>

    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Discover small interior details that can transform the feeling of a room through decorative objects, warm light, textiles and thoughtful styling."
    />
  </head>

  <body>

    <Header />

    <main class="journal-story-page">

      <!-- BREADCRUMB -->

      <div class="product-breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span>·</span>
        <a href="/#journal">Journal</a>
        <span>·</span>
        <span>Small Details That Change a Room</span>
      </div>


      <!-- HERO -->

      <section class="journal-story-hero">

        <p class="product-detail-eyebrow">
          KASODI GUIDE
        </p>

        <h1>
          Small Details That<br />
          Change a Room
        </h1>

        <p class="journal-story-intro">
          A room does not always need a dramatic makeover.
          Sometimes a few thoughtful details are enough to change
          the way the entire space feels.
        </p>

      </section>


      <!-- HERO IMAGE -->

      <section class="journal-story-cover">

        <img
         src="/images/journal/small-details-that-change-a-room-hero.png"
        alt="Warm interior with books, ceramics, flowers and thoughtful decorative details"
        />

      </section>


      <!-- 01 -->

      <section class="journal-story-row journal-story-divider">

        <div class="journal-story-copy">

          <p class="journal-story-number">
            01
          </p>

          <h2>
            Start with what the eye notices first
          </h2>

          <p>
            Every room has places where the eye naturally pauses — a console,
            a bedside table, an empty corner of a shelf or the surface of a chest
            of drawers. These small areas are often the easiest places to introduce
            character without changing the entire room.
          </p>

          <p>
            Choose one object with enough presence to become a quiet focal point.
            It might be an unusual frame, a sculptural vase, a decorative box or
            a piece of glass that catches the light. The object does not need to
            be large; it simply needs a shape, texture or detail worth noticing.
            Give it a little space rather than filling the surface around it.
          </p>

        </div>


        <div class="journal-story-mood">

          <img
           src="/images/journal/small-details-eye-notices-first.png"
           alt="Decorative console with botanical art, books, candle, ceramics and green glass"
          />

        </div>

      </section>


      <!-- 02 -->

      <section class="journal-story-row journal-story-row-product journal-story-divider">

        <div class="journal-inline-product">

          <a href="/new-finds/vintage-botanical-jewelry-box">
            <img
              src="/images/new-finds/vintage-botanical-jewelry-box.png"
              alt="Vintage botanical jewelry box by Tila Home"
            />
          </a>

          <div class="journal-inline-product-info">

            <p class="journal-story-product-category">
              DECORATIVE OBJECTS
            </p>

            <h3>
              Vintage Botanical Jewelry Box
            </h3>

            <p class="journal-story-product-brand">
              Tila Home
            </p>

            <a
              href="/new-finds/vintage-botanical-jewelry-box"
              class="journal-story-discover"
            >
              Discover →
            </a>

          </div>

        </div>


        <div class="journal-story-copy">

          <p class="journal-story-number">
            02
          </p>

          <h2>
            Give everyday surfaces some character
          </h2>

          <p>
            The surfaces we use every day are easy to overlook, yet they have a
            surprisingly strong influence on how a room feels. A bedside table,
            bathroom counter or small shelf can become more considered with just
            two or three objects.
          </p>

          <p>
            Try combining different heights and materials: a decorative box beside
            a small book, a ceramic object next to glass, or something patterned
            against an otherwise quiet background. The composition does not need
            to be perfectly balanced. A slightly irregular arrangement often feels
            more natural, especially when the objects are useful as well as beautiful.
          </p>

        </div>

      </section>


      <!-- 03 -->

      <section class="journal-story-row journal-story-row-product-reverse journal-story-divider">

        <div class="journal-story-copy">

          <p class="journal-story-number">
            03
          </p>

          <h2>
            Change the atmosphere with light
          </h2>

          <p>
            Light can change a familiar room more quickly than almost anything
            else. During the day, allow natural light to create shadows across
            textured surfaces, glass and ceramics. In the evening, smaller pools
            of warm light can make the same space feel softer and more intimate.
          </p>

          <p>
            Candles are especially effective because they introduce both light
            and movement. Even unlit, a sculptural candle can work as a decorative
            object; once lit, it changes the atmosphere completely. You do not
            need many — one or two carefully positioned sources of warm light are
            often enough.
          </p>

        </div>


        <div class="journal-inline-product">

          <a href="/kasodi-edit/sculptural-ivory-candles">
            <img
              src="/images/kasodi-edit/kasodi-edit-sculptural-ivory-candles.png"
              alt="Sculptural ivory candles by ALMA DE LLAMA"
            />
          </a>

          <div class="journal-inline-product-info">

            <p class="journal-story-product-category">
              CANDLES & FRAGRANCE
            </p>

            <h3>
              Sculptural Ivory Candles
            </h3>

            <p class="journal-story-product-brand">
              ALMA DE LLAMA
            </p>

            <a
              href="/kasodi-edit/sculptural-ivory-candles"
              class="journal-story-discover"
            >
              Discover →
            </a>

          </div>

        </div>

      </section>


      <!-- 04 -->

      <section class="journal-story-row journal-story-row-product journal-story-divider">

        <div class="journal-inline-product">

          <a href="/kasodi-edit/embroidered-garden-cushions">
            <img
              src="/images/kasodi-edit/kasodi-edit-embroidered-green-cushions.png"
              alt="Embroidered garden cushions by Running Elephant"
            />
          </a>

          <div class="journal-inline-product-info">

            <p class="journal-story-product-category">
              TEXTILES & COZY
            </p>

            <h3>
              Embroidered Garden Cushions
            </h3>

            <p class="journal-story-product-brand">
              Running Elephant
            </p>

            <a
              href="/kasodi-edit/embroidered-garden-cushions"
              class="journal-story-discover"
            >
              Discover →
            </a>

          </div>

        </div>


        <div class="journal-story-copy">

          <p class="journal-story-number">
            04
          </p>

          <h2>
            Add softness through textiles
          </h2>

          <p>
            Textiles are one of the easiest ways to change a room without changing
            its furniture. A patterned cushion can introduce colour to a neutral
            sofa, while embroidery or visible weaving brings texture to a space
            that feels too smooth or minimal.
          </p>

          <p>
            Avoid making every cushion match. Combining one distinctive design
            with quieter pieces usually feels more collected and relaxed. The same
            idea works with throws and linen. Allow fabrics to look comfortable
            rather than perfectly arranged — softness should make the room feel
            easier to live in, not more formal.
          </p>

        </div>

      </section>


      <!-- 05 + NOTE -->

      <section class="journal-story-closing">

        <div class="journal-story-ending">

          <p class="journal-story-number">
            05
          </p>

          <h2>
            Leave something unexpected
          </h2>

          <p>
            The rooms we remember usually contain something we did not expect to
            see. It might be an ornate vintage-inspired frame in an otherwise
            simple interior, a botanical pitcher used as a vase, coloured glass
            among neutral ceramics or a small decorative object with an unusual shape.
          </p>

          <p>
            There is no need to create several statements at once. One surprising
            object is often enough. Let it sit naturally among quieter pieces and
            allow the contrast to do the work. The most personal homes are rarely
            perfectly coordinated — they contain things chosen because someone
            genuinely liked them.
          </p>

        </div>


        <aside class="journal-story-note">

          <p class="product-detail-eyebrow">
            KASODI NOTE
          </p>

          <h3>
            The smallest details often become the things that make a room feel
            most personal.
          </h3>

        </aside>

      </section>


      <!-- PIECES FOR THE LOOK -->

      <section class="journal-look-edit">

        <div class="journal-look-heading">

          <p class="product-detail-eyebrow">
            KASODI EDIT
          </p>

          <h2>
            Pieces for the Look
          </h2>

          <p>
            Three distinctive details that can bring character, atmosphere
            and softness into a room.
          </p>

        </div>


        <div class="journal-look-grid">


          <article class="journal-look-card">

            <a
              href="/new-finds/vintage-butterfly-photo-frame"
              class="journal-look-image"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/new-finds/vintage-butterfly-photo-frame.png"
                alt="Vintage butterfly photo frame by LEYI DECOR"
              />
            </a>

            <div class="journal-look-info">

              <p class="journal-story-product-category">
                DECORATIVE OBJECTS
              </p>

              <h3>
                Vintage Butterfly Photo Frame
              </h3>

              <p class="journal-story-product-brand">
                LEYI DECOR
              </p>

              <a
                href="/new-finds/vintage-butterfly-photo-frame"
                class="journal-story-discover"
              >
                Discover →
              </a>

            </div>

          </article>


          <article class="journal-look-card">

            <a
              href="/kasodi-edit/sculptural-ivory-candles"
              class="journal-look-image"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/kasodi-edit/kasodi-edit-sculptural-ivory-candles.png"
                alt="Sculptural ivory candles by ALMA DE LLAMA"
              />
            </a>

            <div class="journal-look-info">

              <p class="journal-story-product-category">
                CANDLES & FRAGRANCE
              </p>

              <h3>
                Sculptural Ivory Candles
              </h3>

              <p class="journal-story-product-brand">
                ALMA DE LLAMA
              </p>

              <a
                href="/kasodi-edit/sculptural-ivory-candles"
                class="journal-story-discover"
              >
                Discover →
              </a>

            </div>

          </article>


          <article class="journal-look-card">

            <a
              href="/kasodi-edit/embroidered-garden-cushions"
              class="journal-look-image"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/kasodi-edit/kasodi-edit-embroidered-green-cushions.png"
                alt="Embroidered garden cushions by Running Elephant"
              />
            </a>

            <div class="journal-look-info">

              <p class="journal-story-product-category">
                TEXTILES & COZY
              </p>

              <h3>
                Embroidered Garden Cushions
              </h3>

              <p class="journal-story-product-brand">
                Running Elephant
              </p>

              <a
                href="/kasodi-edit/embroidered-garden-cushions"
                class="journal-story-discover"
              >
                Discover →
              </a>

            </div>

          </article>


        </div>

      </section>


      <!-- FINAL -->

      <section class="journal-article-final">

        <p class="product-detail-eyebrow">
          THE KASODI APPROACH
        </p>

        <h2>
          Change the feeling of a room<br />
          before changing the room itself.
        </h2>

        <p>
          Notice the surfaces, textures, light and small objects already around you.
          Often, a thoughtful detail is enough to make a familiar space feel new.
        </p>

      </section>

    </main>

    <Footer />

  </body>
</html>